WEBVTT

00:01.540 --> 00:04.420
<b>BUNKYU YEAR 3 (1863)</b>

00:18.330 --> 00:19.750
<b>Oh, welcome in!</b>

00:19.750 --> 00:20.750
<b>Hey, Naotsugu.</b>

00:21.000 --> 00:21.750
<b>Greetings.</b>

00:22.170 --> 00:25.130
<b>Jin-dono! You're quite the busy bee these days.</b>

00:25.580 --> 00:27.830
<b>New jobs just keep coming.</b>

00:28.130 --> 00:29.750
<b>Are you going out tonight as well?</b>

00:29.960 --> 00:33.790
<b>Yeah. I caught wind of rumors
about a man-eating demon.</b>

00:34.710 --> 00:38.540
<b>At Mizuho Temple. The same place
that had demon trouble before.</b>

00:39.250 --> 00:40.830
<b>It just never ends, does it?</b>

00:41.580 --> 00:45.920
<b>Times have gotten tough enough already
with the soaring cost of living here in Edo.</b>

00:46.630 --> 00:50.170
<b>The more anxiety among the populace,
the more demons that emerge.</b>

00:52.250 --> 00:57.380
<b>Here you are, Miura-sama.
Thanks for waiting. One order of kake-soba.</b>

01:01.920 --> 01:04.000
<b>Pardon, may I ask something?</b>

01:04.290 --> 01:05.250
<b>What is it?</b>

01:07.790 --> 01:10.920
<b>Why are you the one back there making soba?</b>

02:52.790 --> 02:56.540
<b>Well, you see, the chef offered
to teach me how to make it.</b>

02:56.540 --> 03:01.420
<b>Shucks! We all know he can't
just be a ronin forever, right?</b>

03:02.000 --> 03:04.580
<b>You've learned well, Jinya-kun.</b>

03:04.750 --> 03:05.750
<b>Really?</b>

03:06.040 --> 03:09.710
<b>Yes. You might even be good enough
to open your own shop.</b>

03:11.170 --> 03:12.830
<b>I like the sound of that.</b>

03:13.500 --> 03:14.460
<b>Time to go.</b>

03:18.460 --> 03:19.290
<b>Jinya-kun.</b>

03:21.040 --> 03:22.080
<b>Safe travels.</b>

03:27.290 --> 03:28.420
<b>Please watch your back.</b>

03:32.000 --> 03:35.500
<b>MIZUHO TEMPLE</b>

03:40.710 --> 03:42.500
<b>Been a long time since I was last here.</b>

03:47.130 --> 03:49.250
<b>I don't smell any blood.</b>

04:07.880 --> 04:09.920
<b>So, you must be the man-eating demon.</b>

04:24.130 --> 04:25.920
<b>Won't let me get close, eh?</b>

04:36.460 --> 04:37.380
<b>Skyedge!</b>

04:58.170 --> 04:59.670
<b>Tell me your name.</b>

05:00.580 --> 05:03.000
<b>Yunagi...</b>

05:04.040 --> 05:07.080
<b>I see. Farewell, Yunagi.</b>

05:07.540 --> 05:10.170
<b>I will now consume you and your power.</b>

05:11.170 --> 05:12.000
<b>Assimilation.</b>

05:44.830 --> 05:46.960
<b>Hey, pal! Welcome in.</b>

05:49.290 --> 05:50.830
<b>Greetings, Jin-dono.</b>

05:51.380 --> 05:54.330
<b>Welcome back. You're not hurt, I hope?</b>

05:58.460 --> 06:01.880
<b>It goes without saying.
Jin-dono would never slip up in battle!</b>

06:02.290 --> 06:04.880
<b>I know how skilled Jinya-kun is.</b>

06:05.540 --> 06:08.830
<b>But that doesn't mean he should put himself
in harms way, you know?</b>

06:09.130 --> 06:13.170
<b>Good point. Especially considering
that he has a wife worried for his safety.</b>

06:13.630 --> 06:17.250
<b>Yes. If only he knew how restless she gets.</b>

06:18.580 --> 06:20.380
<b>Yeah, you tell him!</b>

06:20.880 --> 06:25.460
<b>This lummox has no idea how to care for a woman.
There's not a tender bone in his body.</b>

06:26.330 --> 06:28.630
<b>That must be stressful, Yunagi-san.</b>

06:29.330 --> 06:32.460
<b>No kidding. Nothing's worse than an aloof husband.</b>

06:33.170 --> 06:35.540
<b>Although, I am a little jealous.</b>

06:36.170 --> 06:40.630
<b>Jinya-kun has his own brand of kindness.
Not to mention such a cute daughter.</b>

06:41.290 --> 06:45.540
<b>Feel free to adopt her.
I've always hated dealing with kids.</b>

06:46.040 --> 06:49.500
<b>Yunagi-san. Parents shouldn't talk like that!</b>

06:50.080 --> 06:51.250
<b>Yeah, yeah.</b>

06:52.630 --> 06:54.330
<b>"Yunagi"...?</b>

06:55.750 --> 06:56.920
<b>What's the matter?</b>

06:57.500 --> 07:01.130
<b>Oh, my apologies. Just a little surprised.</b>

07:01.670 --> 07:03.080
<b>Who is this child?</b>

07:03.380 --> 07:06.710
<b>Are you sure you're okay?
She's your daughter, obviously.</b>

07:07.790 --> 07:10.380
<b>It's past time that you gave her a name, though.</b>

07:10.920 --> 07:14.330
<b>I'm really awful with stuff like that, so you do it.</b>

07:14.710 --> 07:16.380
<b>Uh, okay.</b>

07:17.330 --> 07:18.750
<b>Something's weird with you.</b>

07:19.290 --> 07:21.250
<b>No, I'm fine.</b>

07:21.790 --> 07:23.040
<b>Uh-huh.</b>

07:23.670 --> 07:26.540
<b>Don't worry. It's nothing, honestly.</b>

07:27.250 --> 07:28.540
<b>Sounds fishy.</b>

07:28.750 --> 07:31.920
<b>It's hard to trust a man who keeps
so many secrets, you know.</b>

07:34.750 --> 07:35.880
<b>Just fibbing!</b>

07:36.250 --> 07:39.040
<b>I was never actually worried in the first place.</b>

07:41.380 --> 07:46.580
<b>Guess not even the great demon hunter
stands a chance against his wife!</b>

07:46.580 --> 07:47.750
<b>That's for sure.</b>

07:50.880 --> 07:52.380
<b>Jinya-kun?</b>

07:52.380 --> 07:55.960
<b>You've been out hunting demons
for multiple nights in a row, pal.</b>

07:55.960 --> 07:58.460
<b>Maybe the fatigue is starting to catch up with you?</b>

07:58.830 --> 08:01.710
<b>You should really allow yourself a day of rest.</b>

08:01.710 --> 08:03.250
<b>No, I can't...</b>

08:06.420 --> 08:13.460
<b>Still, it's a bummer. I was really hoping ya'd get hitched
with Ofuu and carry on the business for me.</b>

08:13.460 --> 08:14.670
<b>Dad!</b>

08:14.920 --> 08:18.830
<b>I mean, that's the whole reason
I started teachin' ya how to make soba.</b>

08:18.830 --> 08:20.540
<b>Oh, is that so?</b>

08:20.540 --> 08:21.830
<b>No!</b>

08:22.040 --> 08:27.080
<b>You gotta tell us the story. How did ya manage
to win over this stubborn mule of a ronin?</b>

08:28.040 --> 08:31.040
<b>Well, it's probably because
we've known each other for so long.</b>

08:31.670 --> 08:33.250
<b>We're from the same village.</b>

08:33.460 --> 08:39.130
<b>There was a hill overlooking a river on the outskirts
of town. That's where I made my move on him.</b>

08:39.580 --> 08:43.170
<b>Oh, how romantic! I'm so envious.</b>

08:43.290 --> 08:48.210
<b>Damn. Friends since childhood, eh?
That's a big advantage.</b>

08:48.920 --> 08:51.630
<b>You both hail from Kadono, right?</b>

08:52.420 --> 08:54.960
<b>There was even a time we lived under the same roof.</b>

08:55.460 --> 08:58.540
<b>Until we had to split up and lived apart afterwards.</b>

08:58.920 --> 09:02.330
<b>So, you know what Jin-dono was like as a kid?</b>

09:02.580 --> 09:03.630
<b>Of course.</b>

09:03.960 --> 09:06.210
<b>He's been a stickler since forever.</b>

09:06.500 --> 09:09.710
<b>"I can't change how I live" is like his catchphrase.</b>

09:09.880 --> 09:13.750
<b>Sounds like Jinya-kun
has always been the awkward type.</b>

09:13.750 --> 09:16.210
<b>Wasn't that frustrating, Yunagi-san?</b>

09:16.630 --> 09:17.880
<b>You bet your bippy.</b>

09:18.330 --> 09:20.170
<b>But I found it kind of charming.</b>

09:20.500 --> 09:22.420
<b>That's why I've stayed with him.</b>

09:23.380 --> 09:28.130
<b>Besides, he's absolutely hopeless
without me around.</b>

09:31.170 --> 09:33.670
<b>Anyway, that was a load of hooey.</b>

09:34.170 --> 09:34.880
<b>Huh?</b>

09:36.080 --> 09:38.420
<b>I lied. About all of it.</b>

09:38.790 --> 09:42.250
<b>You should know it's rude
to pry into people's personal lives.</b>

09:42.750 --> 09:44.420
<b>Well, shall we get going?</b>

09:45.330 --> 09:46.080
<b>Okay.</b>

10:24.000 --> 10:26.500
<b>WOODBLOCK PRINTS</b>

10:24.000 --> 10:26.500
<b>& BOOKS</b>

10:26.880 --> 10:30.710
<b>Among our new releases, "Spirit Tales of Ancient Japan"
has proven very popular.</b>

10:30.880 --> 10:32.330
<b>What's it about?</b>

10:32.750 --> 10:36.380
<b>As the title implies, it's a collection of stories
relating to the supernatural.</b>

10:36.540 --> 10:43.000
<b>Like "Urikohime & the Amanojaku," or "The Invisible
Demon of Teramachi," and other tales yet unheard of.</b>

10:39.500 --> 10:43.250
<b>SPIRIT TALES</b>

10:39.500 --> 10:43.250
<b>OF ANCIENT JAPAN</b>

10:43.250 --> 10:49.630
<b>WOODBLOCK PRINTS</b>

10:43.250 --> 10:49.630
<b>& BOOKS</b>

10:43.420 --> 10:46.500
<b>We also have books like
the "Tenmoku Lovers' Suicide."</b>

10:47.000 --> 10:51.330
<b>It depicts the suffering of a husband
whose wife dies before him.</b>

10:51.670 --> 10:56.540
<b>Uh-huh. Not exactly a good recommendation
for a married couple.</b>

10:56.710 --> 10:59.630
<b>Of course. Aside from that we also have...</b>

11:06.460 --> 11:07.710
<b>Thanks for all your insight.</b>

11:08.170 --> 11:11.290
<b>I have to go for now,
but I'll be back again to borrow some.</b>

11:11.540 --> 11:14.210
<b>Very well. Until next time, then.</b>

11:16.420 --> 11:17.540
<b>Sorry to keep you!</b>

11:17.540 --> 11:18.210
<b>It's fine.</b>

11:21.830 --> 11:25.630
<b>I'm not partial to children. I hate this one in particular.</b>

11:26.420 --> 11:28.380
<b>But it's not like I have a choice.</b>

11:29.000 --> 11:32.330
<b>I can't just leave her with you all the time.</b>

11:33.080 --> 11:35.790
<b>Why the hate? She's your daughter.</b>

11:36.170 --> 11:37.290
<b>Wrong.</b>

11:37.670 --> 11:43.920
<b>Believe it or not, this baby was abandoned
by her parents. I didn't give birth to her.</b>

11:44.670 --> 11:46.500
<b>So I feel no attachment.</b>

11:47.080 --> 11:48.130
<b>Abandoned?</b>

11:48.670 --> 11:50.080
<b>Then why care for her?</b>

11:50.670 --> 11:54.880
<b>More importantly, can we take
a little break? I'm getting tired.</b>

11:59.750 --> 12:02.210
<b>Two cups of tea and an order of dango.</b>

12:02.380 --> 12:05.500
<b>Oh, and some isobe-mochi if you have it.</b>

12:06.790 --> 12:08.130
<b>Someone's upset.</b>

12:08.960 --> 12:13.380
<b>It's not like that. I just can't tell what you're thinking.</b>

12:14.130 --> 12:15.960
<b>Since you do nothing but lie.</b>

12:16.580 --> 12:18.580
<b>Women are born liars.</b>

12:20.830 --> 12:22.080
<b>Thanks for waiting.</b>

12:23.540 --> 12:24.710
<b>Please enjoy yourselves.</b>

12:29.960 --> 12:31.500
<b>I'm surprised you know my tastes.</b>

12:31.500 --> 12:35.210
<b>What do you mean? You're the one
who told me, remember?</b>

12:35.630 --> 12:38.750
<b>You said isobe-mochi was your favorite snack.</b>

12:39.290 --> 12:40.750
<b>Well, let's eat.</b>

12:53.130 --> 12:55.630
<b>Yunagi, are you...?</b>

13:00.750 --> 13:05.290
<b>Ugh, again with the crying. This kid is such a pain.</b>

13:09.040 --> 13:10.250
<b>Did you say something?</b>

13:12.170 --> 13:13.540
<b>Okay, then.</b>

13:13.750 --> 13:17.920
<b>Don't pay me any mind. So, where shall we go next?</b>

13:18.500 --> 13:21.130
<b>There's no point going anywhere special, is there?</b>

13:21.830 --> 13:25.710
<b>We rarely get time to spend like this.
Let's just take it easy.</b>

13:26.080 --> 13:27.920
<b>Together as a family.</b>

13:28.500 --> 13:31.290
<b>All right. Then let's do that.</b>

13:32.420 --> 13:35.630
<b>What do you think this girl's name should be?</b>

13:35.750 --> 13:39.080
<b>Ah... I'm not sure.</b>

13:39.790 --> 13:42.630
<b>Well, you're the one who gets to decide.</b>

13:49.170 --> 13:51.880
<b>So, I read a short story at that bookstore earlier.</b>

13:55.380 --> 14:03.380
<b>Once upon a time, there was an old man and old woman
who lovingly raised a very kind and beautiful daughter.</b>

14:04.040 --> 14:08.830
<b>Until one day, a demon appeared and tricked
the daughter into letting it inside their house.</b>

14:09.420 --> 14:13.170
<b>It was the Amanojaku,
a special type of demon that can lie.</b>

14:14.080 --> 14:16.920
<b>The demon killed the girl and wore her skin,</b>

14:16.920 --> 14:21.460
<b>taking her place and eventually becoming
the bride of a rich husband.</b>

14:22.880 --> 14:25.080
<b>That's the tale of Urikohime & the Amanojaku.</b>

14:25.380 --> 14:27.170
<b>Oh, you've heard of it?</b>

14:27.420 --> 14:29.500
<b>It's a rather famous fable.</b>

14:30.000 --> 14:32.460
<b>Pretty fascinating, isn't it?</b>

14:32.580 --> 14:35.460
<b>Really? Seems like a typical horror story.</b>

14:35.830 --> 14:40.210
<b>Oh, please. You don't understand
the first thing about how to enjoy a good story.</b>

14:40.380 --> 14:44.790
<b>Being able to speculate about
the underlying meaning is what makes it so interesting.</b>

14:46.080 --> 14:47.210
<b>For example...</b>

14:47.750 --> 14:51.210
<b>Why do you suppose
the Amanojaku killed Urikohime?</b>

14:51.290 --> 14:52.420
<b>Why?</b>

14:52.630 --> 14:56.170
<b>Yeah. There is no right answer,
so just give it some thought.</b>

14:57.000 --> 14:57.830
<b>Hmm.</b>

14:59.250 --> 15:02.500
<b>Perhaps because it hated Urikohime?</b>

15:03.630 --> 15:05.420
<b>Sounds plausible to me!</b>

15:05.420 --> 15:09.710
<b>It would actually be pretty interesting
if there had been some kind of vendetta between them.</b>

15:10.040 --> 15:12.250
<b>What's your take on it?</b>

15:12.960 --> 15:14.130
<b>Good question.</b>

15:14.420 --> 15:19.000
<b>Urikohime was on track to live a cushy life with a wealthy
husband-to-be, so it swapped with her out of jealousy.</b>

15:19.330 --> 15:22.040
<b>I think the Amanojaku was a fellow lady.</b>

15:24.330 --> 15:26.580
<b>What? That doesn't click with you?</b>

15:27.000 --> 15:29.710
<b>Actually, that makes a lot of sense...</b>

15:30.040 --> 15:31.080
<b>I know, right?</b>

15:38.420 --> 15:41.960
<b>Oh, hell. I really hate kids.</b>

15:43.960 --> 15:45.460
<b>Spoken like a true Amanojaku.</b>

15:52.420 --> 15:54.130
<b>Adorable, isn't it?</b>

15:54.130 --> 15:55.540
<b>A lucky sparrow.</b>

15:55.830 --> 16:00.250
<b>You're familiar with them?
Sparrows turn into clams, you know.</b>

16:00.460 --> 16:01.830
<b>How does that work?</b>

16:01.830 --> 16:03.380
<b>I'm just fibbing.</b>

16:05.790 --> 16:08.750
<b>Oh, don't give me that look.</b>

16:12.290 --> 16:13.880
<b>The evening calm.</b>

16:15.750 --> 16:21.830
<b>It happens along the coast. The sea breeze blows
during the day, until the land breeze comes at night.</b>

16:22.710 --> 16:28.460
<b>For just a brief period, when the two rotate out,
the wind stops blowing entirely.</b>

16:28.960 --> 16:31.880
<b>And the ocean becomes the very picture of tranquility.</b>

16:32.500 --> 16:34.000
<b>That's my namesake, "Yunagi."</b>

16:34.000 --> 16:36.500
<b>Oh, I'm not lying this time.</b>

16:37.130 --> 16:39.460
<b>Seeing this peaceful sky made me remember.</b>

16:40.040 --> 16:45.170
<b>The evening calm turns the ocean
as clear as a mirror. It's truly beautiful.</b>

16:46.000 --> 16:48.170
<b>I hope to see it again some day.</b>

16:49.040 --> 16:51.830
<b>With you, if possible.</b>

16:53.630 --> 16:55.080
<b>Are you crying?</b>

16:55.880 --> 16:58.080
<b>The sunset just got in my eyes for a second.</b>

17:00.040 --> 17:01.960
<b>The sky of the evening calm, eh?</b>

17:02.710 --> 17:05.630
<b>I suppose that means the dusk is your golden hour.</b>

17:05.790 --> 17:07.290
<b>Are you being serious?</b>

17:07.500 --> 17:09.880
<b>I didn't peg you as one for sappy lines like that.</b>

17:21.960 --> 17:23.750
<b>Wow, those are pretty.</b>

17:24.290 --> 17:25.830
<b>The white-powder flower.</b>

17:26.210 --> 17:29.000
<b>Also known as the "four o'clock flower"
or "nighttime beauty."</b>

17:29.330 --> 17:33.000
<b>White-powder? But I can see pink and yellow ones, too.</b>

17:33.380 --> 17:36.170
<b>It's because of the white powder inside the seed husk.</b>

17:36.750 --> 17:40.420
<b>Apparently, children would use it
like makeup to play pretend.</b>

17:41.500 --> 17:46.710
<b>And for some reason, these flowers evolved
to only open from late afternoon to dusk.</b>

17:47.000 --> 17:48.670
<b>Aren't you just the know-it-all?</b>

17:48.670 --> 17:50.040
<b>I'm merely repeating what I've heard.</b>

17:50.420 --> 17:55.580
<b>Still, what a funny flower.
Nighttime is such an odd time to bloom.</b>

17:56.250 --> 17:57.290
<b>Indeed.</b>

18:10.960 --> 18:11.790
<b>Yunagi.</b>

18:14.330 --> 18:15.880
<b>I had a great time today.</b>

18:16.290 --> 18:17.830
<b>Why're you acting all sentimental?</b>

18:18.420 --> 18:20.830
<b>I'm not. These are my honest feelings.</b>

18:21.710 --> 18:24.420
<b>That grouchy look of yours says otherwise.</b>

18:24.420 --> 18:28.630
<b>That's just how I look. I'm not lying to you.</b>

18:29.750 --> 18:32.670
<b>There was a time I used to dream about a life like this.</b>

18:33.540 --> 18:37.830
<b>Passing my days idly by
with the woman who I fell in love with.</b>

18:38.750 --> 18:41.830
<b>I can only imagine how blissful it would have been.</b>

18:44.750 --> 18:48.460
<b>Hey. Will you call my name for me?</b>

18:59.380 --> 19:00.420
<b>Jinta.</b>

19:01.460 --> 19:02.880
<b>Is that what you wanted?</b>

19:05.460 --> 19:06.790
<b>Thank you.</b>

19:11.210 --> 19:13.460
<b>To be honest, I'm consumed with regret.</b>

19:14.210 --> 19:18.790
<b>If only I had done a better job,
then maybe Shirayuki would still be alive.</b>

19:20.170 --> 19:22.500
<b>But it wasn't meant to be.</b>

19:23.790 --> 19:28.580
<b>Shirayuki, my dad, and Natsu...
things could have ended differently.</b>

19:30.040 --> 19:33.420
<b>The truth is, I've been lamenting it all along.</b>

19:34.460 --> 19:37.080
<b>Is this your power at work?</b>

19:37.080 --> 19:38.630
<b>Or maybe it's...</b>

19:40.040 --> 19:42.380
<b>just my sorrow coming to the forefront.</b>

19:43.830 --> 19:47.920
<b>I knew it all along. You weren't the demon who was lying.</b>

19:48.920 --> 19:50.500
<b>I'm the real Amanojaku.</b>

19:53.330 --> 19:55.750
<b>It's impossible for you to be here in the first place.</b>

19:56.670 --> 19:59.380
<b>Yunagi. I was the one who...</b>

20:01.250 --> 20:03.960
<b>Don't be silly, you didn't kill me.</b>

20:04.130 --> 20:04.960
<b>But...</b>

20:07.040 --> 20:11.170
<b>Because the truth is that I don't exist anywhere at all.</b>

20:11.880 --> 20:16.750
<b>Our marriage, all those memories,
even my presence here...</b>

20:16.960 --> 20:18.630
<b>Everything was a lie.</b>

20:20.250 --> 20:23.170
<b>So you shouldn't let it bother you.</b>

20:26.710 --> 20:27.880
<b>Anyways, it's a relief.</b>

20:28.630 --> 20:31.250
<b>I'm glad that a kindhearted soul like you showed up.</b>

20:38.330 --> 20:43.790
<b>Like I said, I hate kids. So you're in charge of her now.</b>

20:46.830 --> 20:51.380
<b>It's all right. I know that you'll raise her well.</b>

21:07.130 --> 21:09.790
<b>Bye-bye. See you again someday.</b>

21:34.710 --> 21:38.040
<b>The ability to create illusions that deceive others.</b>

21:38.750 --> 21:42.920
<b>And the illusions are all linked with the user's memories.</b>

21:43.920 --> 21:45.210
<b>"Falsehood."</b>

21:45.790 --> 21:49.750
<b>Now I get it. That was Yunagi's demonic power.</b>

21:58.880 --> 22:02.500
<b>The fox and the flames were just visions Yunagi created.</b>

22:03.670 --> 22:05.250
<b>Actually, it goes further...</b>

22:16.420 --> 22:18.960
<b>There was never a "man-eating demon" in the first place.</b>

22:23.750 --> 22:28.130
<b>That was just a lie meant to make someone realize
this child had been abandoned here.</b>

22:29.830 --> 22:31.790
<b>She made quite the Amanojaku.</b>

22:32.880 --> 22:39.000
<b>Yunagi. In that moment, you were truly
the mother this child needed.</b>

22:43.080 --> 22:45.130
<b>A flower that blooms in the evening calm.</b>

22:46.080 --> 22:48.040
<b>That's what I'll name you after, "Nomari."</b>

22:55.630 --> 22:58.580
<b>One day, I'll tell you all about her.</b>

23:00.170 --> 23:04.830
<b>Your kind-hearted mother
who pretended to be the Amanojaku.</b>

23:12.580 --> 23:15.080
<b>Oh, hey, pal! Welcome i- huh?</b>

23:15.460 --> 23:16.210
<b>Wha-?!</b>

23:16.420 --> 23:19.460
<b>Uh, Jinya-kun? Why do you have that baby?</b>

23:20.920 --> 23:21.830
<b>Oh...</b>

23:23.920 --> 23:28.710
<b>Are you sure you're okay?
She's your daughter, obviously.</b>

23:37.080 --> 23:39.420
<b>This is my daughter.</b>
